<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">al-Qaeda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1988">1988</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Al-Qaida, al-Qaida</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Qaeda is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> jihadist organisation founded in 1988 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osama-bin-laden">Osama bin Laden</a> and other veterans of the war against the Soviets in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>. Based in Taliban-ruled Afghanistan in the late 1990s, it carried out the attacks of 11 September 2001, which led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> invasion of Afghanistan. Its regional branches have operated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahel">Sahel</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/al-qaeda.jpg" alt="al-Qaeda" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Jihad.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Militant jihadism opened a further front: <b>al-Qaeda</b> bombed the USS Cole in Aden harbour in October 2000, killing seventeen American sailors, and Al-Qaeda in the Arabian Peninsula, formed in 2009, became a target of American drone strikes.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-yemen">Republic of Yemen · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>…drew accusations of sponsoring terrorism, sharpened when fifteen of the September 11 hijackers proved to be Saudi nationals and answered by the Grand Mufti's 2014 fatwa against ISIS and <b>al-Qaeda</b> and the Islamic Military Counter Terrorism Coalition of 2015; since 2016 the state has stopped funding mosques abroad.</blockquote><a href="/empire/saudi-arabia">Saudi Arabia · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Al-Qaeda</b> formally declared the “far enemy” under attack in 1996, and Osama bin Laden’s terror attacks climaxed in the September 11 attacks of 2001.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/islamism">Islamism · In Power</a></li><li><blockquote>Navy SEALs raided a compound in Abbottabad and killed the <b>al-Qaeda</b> leader behind the 11 September attacks.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/may-1">1 May in history</a></li><li><blockquote>American and British forces began bombing Taliban and <b>al-Qaeda</b> targets in Afghanistan, four weeks after the 11 September attacks.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/october-7">7 October in history</a></li><li><blockquote>It hosted Osama bin Laden and <b>al-Qaeda</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/islamic-emirate-of-afghanistan-1996-2001">Islamic Emirate of Afghanistan (1996-2001)</a></li></ul></section>
